  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Progressive left-sided hearing reduction and left-sided facial numbness for ~3 weeks.\n- Symptoms (onset/duration/severity/aggravating/alleviating): Onset ~3 weeks ago; persistent left-sided facial numbness around left ear and jawline, reduced hearing on left, occasional tinnitus (ringing) and occasional dizziness associated with ringing. No ear pain, no discharge, no fever. Symptoms are ongoing and impacting work (jockey) by causing dizziness with ringing. No clear alleviating factors noted.\n- Past medical history: Nasal polyps (intermittently symptomatic); remote history of 'labyrinthitis' (patient unsure of details).\n- Medications/allergies: Intermittent nasal steroid spray (prescription, name unknown); occasional antacid (Rennies). Allergy: latex.\n- Family/social history: Brother with neurofibromatosis (type not specified). Lives with partner. Occupation: jockey. No pets. Smoking/alcohol not documented.\n- Vital signs/exam findings: No vitals documented. No physical exam findings recorded (video consult only). Doctor planned in-person neurological and ear exam.\n- Labs/imaging: None reported or performed.",
